        "by": "human",
        "reason": "attempt_0003/concept.sql:35 maps Observation.effective_datetime through CAST(TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP(REPLACE(REGEXP_REPLACE(...)), pinned-format) AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ). The offset-aware parser re-renders the instant in spark.sql.session.timeZone and the pinned format silently NULLs any shape it misses, so the recorded exact match holds only at session zone America/New_York and is not reproducible elsewhere. attempt_0002 had ALREADY removed this construction; attempt_0003 reintroduced it. Replace with a bare TRY_CAST(o.effective_datetime AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ), nothing wrapped around it. charttime is load-bearing beyond its own column here: it is stringified into the UUIDv5 that witnesses 'No Response-ETT', so verify that discriminator still fires. mimic_utils validate-demo now refuses this construction (sql_lint datetime-parser).",
