        "by": "human",
        "reason": "attempt_0005/concept.sql states a value where FHIR carries none: for itemid 223900 served as Quantity 1 it scores gcs_verbal = 1, giving 576,086 differing_conflict rows, zero differing_null_only, and no NULL on any column. That is the estimate-instead-of-an-absence failure of LOOP_CONTRACT.md:406-411 -- it manufactures the conflict that forces the contested tier, then has to argue its own approximation is intrinsic, which it cannot, because the typed NULL was available. The judge's essential-loss finding at mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_observation_chartevents.sql:69-80 is UPHELD and is not what is being reopened; the ruling was passed a port that states values it does not have. Re-port emitting typed NULL for gcs and gcs_verbal wherever an itemid-223900 observation is served as Quantity 1 at this charttime or at the previous one inside the six-hour window (678,748 of 1,637,763 rows, probe job 30309450), and gcs_unable as 100% NULL declared in unrepresentable.json. No ventilation-status substitution: measured 4.7% recall from oxygen_delivery and 80.1% accuracy from the oracle ventilation table (job 30309569), both estimates rather than mappings. Rationale and numbers in human_override/gcs.md; upstream fix filed as kind-lab/mimic-fhir#125.",
